# Dolunay golden-model skeleton — headless smoke test.
#
# Renode registers types only from its own installation directory, so the build
# output has to be copied there first (DECISIONS.md D8). From this directory:
#
#   RENODE_BIN=<unpacked renode tree> dotnet build model
#   cp build/plugin/Dolunay.Model.dll build/plugin/Dolunay.Renode.dll "$RENODE_BIN/"
#   timeout -k 5 60 renode --disable-xwt --console --plain run.resc
#
# Passes if Renode prints the PC (0x1000) and quits: the platform names
# CPU.Dolunay, which exists only if the DLLs were found. Nothing here asserts
# machine behaviour; that is not decided yet (CONTRACT.md §2).

mach create "dolunay"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @Dolunay.repl

cpu PC
quit
